{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords","kind":"definition","title":"The $q$-Reeb flow in color-sector coordinates","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-color-sector-coords","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-bundle","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-flow"],"tags":["reeb-flow","color-sectors","exceptional-divisor","substrate-parameter"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalReeb.QReebFlowOnColorCoords","text":"q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords.md","leanSource":"q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{r}(\\phi,\\psi), \\mathfrak{g}(\\phi,\\psi), \\mathfrak{b}(\\phi,\\psi)</code> be the color-sector parametrisation on the Reeb bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R}_p</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Reeb flow</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\phi^q_t</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t \\in [0,\\pi]</code>, acts on the red sector by</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\phi^q_t \\cdot \\mathfrak{r}(\\phi,\\psi) \\;=\\; \\mathfrak{r}(\\phi,\\,\\psi + k^{(r)}\\,q\\,t),</code></pre>\n<p>and on the green and blue sectors by the analogous equations with rate multipliers <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k^{(g)}, k^{(b)} \\in \\mathbb{Z}</code>. The braid generator determines the signed rate multiplier <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k^{(s)}</code>: a spectator sector has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k^{(s)} = 0</code>; in a two-strand subsystem the active leading strand has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k^{(s)} = +1</code> and the partner strand has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k^{(s)} = -1</code>; a uniform-vortex 3-cycle generator applies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k = +1</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k = -1</code> to all sectors simultaneously.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.11.8","page":"b/def-q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.QReebFlowOnColorCoords","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
